  "question": {
    "text": "The compound with molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6$, which gives only one monobromo derivative and takes up four moles of hydrogen per mole for complete hydrogenation has ________ $=$ electrons.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since 4 moles of $\\mathrm{H}_2$ is being added for complete hydrogenation the degree of unsaturation $=4$\n\nNo. of $\\pi$ electrons in $\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_6=4 \\times 2=8$",
    "image": null
  },
